    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by the high-upside pairing of **Kyle Tucker** (77.08) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.85). **Kyle Tucker** sits at the top of our daily efficiency rankings, benefitting significantly from a soft matchup against Young (xERA 4.79) and a substantial SP Skill boost. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** thrives in his matchup against Martinez, N, where a favorable dynamic platoon advantage and a premium spot at the top of the order drive his high score. **Andy Pages** (72.55) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.90) also present strong value, as both capitalize on weak opposing arms and high-leverage lineup positions to solidify our offensive floor against favorable pitching matchups.\n\nStrategic lineup construction required a difficult decision at the margins, with **Wade Meckler** (52.57) ultimately yielding his spot despite a favorable park factor against Perkins. While **Wade Meckler** offered intrigue, the sheer efficiency of **Cole Carrigg** (62.83) in a hitter-friendly environment ultimately pushed him into the starting OF1 slot. We remain cautious regarding **Jackson Merrill** (57.18) and **Jacob Wilson** (54.18); both face elite-level arms in Eovaldi and Detmers, respectively, which heavily suppressed their base projections. We are monitoring these games closely for any late weather alerts, as the risk of underperformance against these tougher pitchers makes them the first candidates for benching should our late-afternoon options show superior availability. **Coby Mayo** (38.51) remains firmly on the bench, failing to clear our 40.0 efficiency floor against Sheehan, ensuring we reserve our limited game caps for more high-probability scoring scenarios.",
